- **Always write in GitHub-flavored Markdown.** Every bead **description** (`-d`) and every
  **comment** you add must be valid markdown — headings, **bold**, `inline code`, fenced code blocks,
  lists and links so it reads well in the UI. Preserve real line breaks with `$'...'` (real `\n`) or,
  for anything multi-line, pipe via stdin (`printf '%s' "$c" | bd comment <id> --stdin`) — never
  collapse a comment into one flat line.
